# Third-party notices

This crate is pure Rust. The **default build links no native/C libraries** — it
does not vendor the AppImage runtime, libfuse, or squashfuse. It depends only on
permissively licensed Rust crates (MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSD / zlib), notably:

- [`backhand`](https://crates.io/crates/backhand) — SquashFS reader/writer (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
- [`object`](https://crates.io/crates/object) — ELF parsing (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
- [`fuser`](https://crates.io/crates/fuser), Linux only — FUSE protocol in pure Rust, built without its `libfuse` features (MIT)
- [`flate2`](https://crates.io/crates/flate2) (MIT OR Apache-2.0) + [`zlib-rs`](https://crates.io/crates/zlib-rs) (Zlib) — gzip, pure Rust
- [`lz4_flex`](https://crates.io/crates/lz4_flex), [`rust-lzo`](https://crates.io/crates/rust-lzo) — lz4 / lzo, pure Rust

`fuser` mounts with `mount(2)` and, for an unprivileged user, asks the system's
`fusermount3` helper at runtime; the helper is not linked or redistributed by
this crate.

The optional `launcher` feature adds [`signal-hook`](https://crates.io/crates/signal-hook)
(Apache-2.0 OR MIT) and uses [`libc`](https://crates.io/crates/libc) (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Directory operations use [`cap-std`](https://crates.io/crates/cap-std) and
[`cap-tempfile`](https://crates.io/crates/cap-tempfile) (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT). [`same-file`](https://crates.io/crates/same-file) checks
directory identity (Unlicense OR MIT).

## Optional decoders

The non-default `xz` and `zstd` features add pure-Rust SquashFS decompression:

- `xz` → [`lzma-rs`](https://crates.io/crates/lzma-rs) (MIT)
- `zstd` → [`ruzstd`](https://crates.io/crates/ruzstd) (MIT)

These features add reading support; packing supports gzip, LZ4, LZO, and uncompressed payloads.
